  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper evaluates a hybrid classical–quantum neural network using simulated variational circuits (≈8 qubits, 8 layers) for credit‑scoring and MNIST classification. On the finance dataset the best hybrid model reaches test AUC 0.72 versus a classical neural network’s 0.77, while on MNIST both models achieve about 0.81 test accuracy (QNet 0.98/0.81 train/test vs NNet 0.83/0.81). All results are obtained on noiseless simulators using TensorFlow Quantum.",
